    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0705" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Austria/13</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Acting Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-05-09">May 9, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I called in the Austrian Minister<anchor n="3" xml:id="d358-f1"/> to hand him the
                    agreement as to the moratorium, a copy of which is attached.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d358-f2"/> He said that he knew these agreements had been given to
                    others and was beginning to hope that Austria had been forgotten. I pointed out
                    to him the necessity of haste in signing it to avoid complications and explained
                    to him that it was, after all, a routine matter. The Minister said he would
                    telegraph his Government, asking that he be appointed to sign.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. R. Castle, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
